abstract: >-
  Dockerized Python engine for daily wildfire-danger mapping in Galicia, Spain.
  It fetches terrain, fuel, Sentinel-2, Sentinel-3 LST, infrastructure, land-cover
  and MeteoGalicia weather inputs into PostGIS, computes the Canadian Fire Weather
  Index, scores each factor and aggregates them with the Analytic Hierarchy
  Process into continuous and classified danger maps with input-coverage rasters,
  served through a FastAPI service. Developed within the STORCITO project, funded
  by the European Union's Horizon Europe programme under grant agreement
  No. 101182153.
keywords:
  - wildfire danger
  - Galicia
  - Fire Weather Index
  - Analytic Hierarchy Process
